1
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:06,000
The story of two bands, one girl and a night they will never forget.

2
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:06,000
Spike Island is a comedy, drama, music film directed by Mat Whitecross.

3
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:06,000
Teenage musicians travel to England's Spike Island in the hope of attending an
outdoor performance by their favorite band, the Stone Roses.

4
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:06,000
Tits, played by Elliott Tittensor.

5
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:06,000
Sally, played by Emilia Clarke.

6
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:06,000
Dodge, played by Nico Mirallegro.

7
00:42:00,000 --> 00:42:06,000
Little Gaz, played by Adam Long.

8
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
Zippy, played by Jordan Murphy.

9
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
Penfold, played by Oliver Heald.

10
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
Spike Island is a 2012 British comedy film directed by Mat
Whitecross and written by Chris Coghill.

11
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
It was distributed by Universal Pictures and Vertigo Films
and produced by Revolver Entertainment.

12
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
The film is based on the Stone Roses' seminal gig on Spike Island in Widnes, Cheshire, England, and follows the story of a group of friends who
idolise the band and try to get into the gig, but are faced with problems because they don't have tickets or a way to get there.

13
01:18:00,000 --> 01:18:06,000
Spike Island premiered on 11 October 2012 at the BFI London Film
Festival and was released on DVD on 21 June 2013.

14
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
The film explores themes of ecstasy, liverpool, england,
cannabis, pot smoking, music business.

15
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:06,000
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
